WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.750
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.750
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.750
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:44.090
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:44.090
Chapter 8

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:54.420
In early June, as Whitsunday comes near,
the streets of Odin become festive.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:59.280
It was originally a day for an
important religious ceremony...

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:05.300
...but has now become an occasion to eat,
drink and be merry on a nice early summer day.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:15.180
Siegfried Kircheis returned home
for the first time in eight years...

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.710
...on June 9th,
the eve of Whitsunday.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:24.680
Since Reinhard had to attend a Ministry of Military party...

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.210
...where only admirals and
their wives were invited...

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:32.770
...he urged Kircheis to use that opportunity to
return home as he had recommended before.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.810
What would you
like, young man ?

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.650
Black beer in a large glass.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.080
A bit of sausage and potatoes.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.480
And sauerkraut, too.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.480
I'll use the phone.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:05.130
If they're not at home, I'll be content
to just look at the house from the outside.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.840
Hello, Mother ?

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.300
It's Siegfried.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.250
Yes, I'm thinking
about coming home now.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:15.770
Yes.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:16.890
Yes.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.020
I'm already in town.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.130
Yes.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.300
About thirty
minutes from home.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.000
Yes.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.080
I'll see you later.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:30.470
Oh, yes !

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:34.320
You're the red-headed boy
from the Kircheis's place.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.300
It's been a long time, Master.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.000
You've grown so big.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.210
Your head almost
touches the ceiling.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:49.680
Kircheis was planning to prepare himself
emotionally for his return home at this pub...

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:57.030
...with a glass of black beer to allay his shyness,
mixed with his nostalgia for coming home.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.300
Welcome home, Siegfried.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.540
I'm home, Father, Mother.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.660
I wonder if Mother
was always this small ?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.360
You're truly
such a bad boy.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.120
If you had told me yesterday, I would
have cooked plenty of good food.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.640
You didn't even give
me time to prepare.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.470
I'm sorry.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:42.930
I decided out
of the blue.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.940
I wonder if Father's hand
was always this small and thin ?

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.190
So how has it been ?

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.730
Is the heir of the
Musels treating you well ?

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.790
He's been marvelous to me.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:02.840
There's nothing
to worry about.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.240
Dinner will be ready soon.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.030
It's the same as it
was eight years ago.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:22.210
But for you to have
joined the military...

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:26.770
...since you're such a kindhearted
boy, I still can't believe it now.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.260
Even if you're kindhearted
toward certain people...

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:36.150
...you can be cruel and unsympathetic
to other people, Mother.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:41.470
More importantly,
how are the orchids ?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:48.670
With the help of the money you sent me last
year, we were able to rebuild the greenhouse.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:49.230
How about it ?

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:51.030
Do you want
to take a look ?

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.820
I recommended saving
it up for our retirement.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:03.250
But Father apparently isn't thinking
about anything but the orchids.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:06.970
After our retirement,
we'll receive pensions.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.570
Besides, if worst comes to
worst, we can sell the orchids.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:13.030
But you know, ten
years down the road...

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:16.010
...Siegfried will marry someone
and bring grandchildren to our home.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:20.580
If we can't do anything then,
it would really be a shame.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.990
At least the principle
money for a housing loan...

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:24.960
I don't plan
on getting married.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.580
Ah, well, I mean,
not for a while.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.220
I haven't given it much thought.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.580
Also, Father didn't marry
until he was past 30.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:42.300
You're right, but if you already have someone
in mind, you don't have to wait till you're 30.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.730
Aren't you seeing anyone ?

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.020
Um, I'm not seeing
anyone at the moment, so...

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.710
By the way, what happened
to the house next door ?

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:08.640
Right now, a retired officer named
Beckman and his wife are living there.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:12.680
But it seems they don't have enough hands,
so the house isn't as well-kept as it was before...

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.230
...and it is a little bit untidy.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:17.190
But it's not something
we can meddle in.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:31.960
In that house, other people are
living, spending their lives...

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.080
Listen, Siegfried...

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.560
What is it, Mother ?

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.900
Are you sure you're not regretting
having joined the military ?

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.730
I have no regrets, Mother.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.910
I see.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.410
Then that's fine.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.260
It's a rewarding job.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:04.790
And I don't think I've done anything to be
ashamed of, for myself and for other people.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:10.020
Also, I'll confidently predict that by the
time you see your grandchildren...

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:12.710
...the war with the
rebels will be over.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:25.480
It's gotten so late now.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.230
Go to sleep now.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.540
I've bought new
pajamas for you.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.380
Thank you.

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:32.730
Good night.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.200
Shall I visit it tomorrow ?

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:13.990
Before, I used to feel as though this bed
was as big as half of the entire universe.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.150
Well, I'm going now.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.040
Take care.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.680
Try not to catch cold.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:32.650
Colds are the source
of ten thousand diseases.

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:34.300
Yes, I know.

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:37.160
Take care of yourselves,
Father, Mother.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:46.540
It is ill-kept.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:54.130
This house was old even when
the Musels were living here...

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:57.810
...but Lady Annerose
kept it well-maintained.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:06.370
The eldest son, Karl, died
in battle in 480, at age 24.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:10.730
The second son, Isaac, died
in battle in 484, at age 25.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:16.460
The third son, Johann, died
in battle in 484, at age 22.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.030
Their last son.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.470
I can't blame them.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:33.580
No one has the
right to blame them.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:43.680
I became a soldier, there
have been many battles...

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:47.400
...and I've witnessed
many deaths firsthand.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:54.150
In exchange for my own survival, I've
accumulated many deaths around myself.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.360
I cannot forget that fact.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:59.470
You must be Siegfried Kircheis.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.360
Martin ?

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:09.140
Are you Martin Bufholtz ?

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.220
So you're attending a university.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:19.320
Yeah, I'm majoring in classics
at Odin National University.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:22.150
That suits you so well.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:27.450
When we were little, my mother used to say
that you'd become a good scholar someday.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:29.860
Thanks.

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:35.210
But anyway, Siegfried, I would have never
imagined back then that you'd join the military.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:43.090
But of course, I'll have to join the army
the year after next, too, since I'll turn 20.

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:44.960
It's compulsory
service for two years.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:48.190
Unlike you, I'll start from the
bottom, as a second-class soldier.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:52.840
If I survive for a year, I heard
I'd be promoted to first-class...

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.460
...but I'll probably have
died in battle by then.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.490
Martin...

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:00.680
I'm sorry, Siegfried.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:03.300
I'm not trying
to be sarcastic.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.540
I know.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.430
Don't worry.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:12.560
But for those who are engaged in some
form of research at a national university...

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.690
...there's the privilege of exemption
from military service, isn't there ?

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.160
Didn't you apply for it ?

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:19.600
Of course I did.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:21.730
But it was turned down.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:23.840
If it were medicine or engineering,
they would have accepted it...

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:28.850
...but for a "useless" field like literature,
they say there's no privilege of exemption.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.610
Literature is a "useless"
field of study ?

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:36.480
Of course, I don't think that way, but
I'm not the one who makes the decision.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:39.710
The officers at the Ministry of Military
Affairs are the ones who do it.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:46.230
Those bastards in their comfortable office
chairs not only send us to the front lines...

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.680
...but also presume to rank the
fields of the studies and the arts.{in accordance with what they think is useful}

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:52.380
What a commendable
bunch of people.

00:13:54.620 --> 00:14:00.150
Such a social system that allows those
people to wield authority won't last forever.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:06.060
You may be right, but it's not something
that'll change in just two years.

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:13.150
By the way, are you still
with Reinhard von Musel...

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:16.280
...that absurdly strong-willed
transfer student ?

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:22.060
And he's getting
promoted smoothly ?

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.380
He recently became
a Rear Admiral.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.580
I see.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.150
As I thought.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:29.610
He's suited to be a
high-ranking military official.

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.920
He can be cool
no matter who dies.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:37.840
He's so proud, like he
doesn't know who he is.

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:42.850
I might well be forced to the
killing fields under Lord Musel.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:45.030
Martin.

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:50.520
The gentleman named Reinhard von Musel is my superior and he's an important person to me.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:52.790
And he's very good to me.

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:55.720
So could you not speak
ill of him in my presence ?

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:57.580
I'm sorry.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.150
I didn't mean
to be malicious.

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:01.330
I'm not trying
to argue with you.

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:02.490
Forgive me.

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:04.000
I'm fine as long as
we understand each other.

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:13.490
I'm glad we met today.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.670
Me, too.

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:17.030
It was good
to see you.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:23.700
I was being a
little melancholy.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:24.680
I know.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:28.240
But until the day I'm drafted,
I'll live more positively.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:31.460
Till then, I want to finish
the essay I'm working on now...

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:35.160
...and make it the proof that I
accomplished something in my lifetime.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.330
I think that's a
marvelous thing to do.

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:40.940
I want you to
read the essay.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.920
I don't care if you don't
understand the content of it.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:48.500
To have someone read it - I want
to use that goal as my motivation.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:52.100
If it's okay, I'll
be happy to read it.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:56.030
Well then.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:58.610
When the time comes,
I'll see you again.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:03.570
But the two never
saw each other again.

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:08.780
Six months later, when the Military Police arrested the members of an underground anti-war organization...

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:13.080
...Martin Bufholtz
was among those arrested.

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:16.740
Despite the pang in his heart, Kircheis couldn't
help but understand why that had to happen.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.680
Furthermore,
two years later...

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:25.300
...by which time Kircheis' position
and authority had strengthened...

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:31.610
...he investigated Martin's whereabouts, and
found out that Martin had died of malnutrition...

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:35.130
...in an internment camp
for political offenders.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:02.640
Sorry to be late.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:05.790
What, you're back already ?

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.660
You could have
taken your time.

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:10.470
What have you been doing ?

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:12.970
In the morning, I
listened to music a little.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:17.500
And then I researched comparative studies
on stratagems - Borden's and Eckhardt's.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.610
I see.

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:22.010
Because there was no one to
bother me, I was really productive.

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.500
That's a good
thing once in a while.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.990
Since I was late,
he's pouting.

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:29.510
I bought Frankfurterklantz.

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.150
Won't you have some ?

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.260
No.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.160
You don't like it ?

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:39.640
You think you can appease me with cake -
I don't like your scheming disposition.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:44.540
This cake is so good that it will more
than compensate for my disposition.

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:47.990
I will ask Mrs. Hoover
to make some coffee.

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:51.400
If you are willing to forgive
me, please come downstairs.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:12.560
Right now, at this moment,
maybe I'm truly happy.

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:24.680
On June 11th, ministry general staff officer
and court advisor, Admiral Grimmelshausen...

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:29.640
...paid a visit to the Kaiser's palace, Neue
Sanssouci, to pay his respects to the Kaiser.

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:37.480
By the way, about Reinhard von
Musel, who served under you...

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:38.950
What do you
think of him ?

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:43.280
Ah, let's see...

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:48.470
Oh, you mean the brother
of Countess Grunewald.

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:58.150
When I see him, I can easily imagine how
beautiful his sister the Countess must be.

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:07.640
Youth is such a splendid commodity,
don't you think, Your Majesty ?

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:13.050
When I see him,
I truly believe it.

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:17.130
There seems to be nothing that's
impossible in this universe.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:20.450
I agree with you,
Grimmelshausen.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:25.380
Of things that are humanly possible,
there's probably nothing that he can't do.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:29.260
Except for specialized
studies or arts.

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.300
Yes, I believe so.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:40.380
To tell the truth, Grimmelshausen,
his ancestry is merely <i>Reichsritter...</i>

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:44.280
...and since he's only 18
it's not much of an issue now.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.880
But before he
becomes an adult...

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:52.420
...I'm thinking about bestowing a legitimate
aristocratic family name on him.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:57.340
You're planning to provide
him with such prestige ?

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.760
I don't know.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:04.360
The one that receives the prestige may
be the family name, rather than him.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:09.380
In any case, what do
you think of my idea ?

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:13.910
I think it's
a splendid idea.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:18.160
"Splendid," eh ?

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:20.750
I think so, too.

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:30.690
Court is an ideal place for
breeding rumors and gossip.

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:35.280
It didn't take a day for the Kaiser's
plan to reach Reinhard's ear.

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:38.870
The Kaiser instructed the
Imperial Household Agency...

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:43.380
...to allow me to inherit an aristocratic
family name when I turn 20.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:47.870
There are several candidates among
the families that don't have successors.

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:51.860
The Brentanos, the
Essenbachs, the Lohengramms...

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.010
I think there
are several others.

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:59.950
It's rare for Lord Reinhard to be as pleased
with the Kaiser's favors as he is now.

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:08.550
But the elitist lineage aristocrats won't
be happy when they hear about this.

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:10.910
Their strong hostility
is inevitable.

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:16.540
As was thought, the lineage
aristocrats were enraged.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:21.760
The Countship of Lohengramm is a famed
lineage family since the time of Kaiser Rudolph.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:25.270
It's an outrage, to bestow that dignified
name upon a social-climbing brat.

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:28.680
Since when have the names of
distinguished Imperial aristocratic families...

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:30.690
...become merchandise
for social-climbers ?

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:36.040
That anger was also, naturally, directed
toward the decision-maker, Friedrich IV.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:44.490
He never studied imperialism as a child and only made a name for himself as a total dissipate.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:47.190
And now, he doesn't 
even give consideration...

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:49.900
...to the long exchange between
aristocrats and the royal family.

00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:50.840
What a pity !

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:57.680
If a commoner uttered a statement like
that, they would be immediately executed...

00:21:57.680 --> 00:22:02.540
...but a distinguished aristocrat wouldn't be questioned, even if the statement is made in public.

00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:09.780
Distinguished aristocrats have a twisted mentality to consider family ranks as spiritual possessions.

00:22:10.920 --> 00:22:15.420
While the topic of Reinhard's succession to an
aristocratic family incited discontent like this...

00:22:15.420 --> 00:22:19.510
...there was another strange
rumor circulating in the court.

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:24.080
It concerned Hermann von
Luneberg's background.

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:30.490
That "Luneberg" was his mother's name,
and his father is from the Goldenbaum family...

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:35.750
...and when he found out the secret of his
birth, he defected back to the Empire...

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:38.700
...with the ambition of
succeeding to the royal family.

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:45.250
It's an interesting story, but
there's no substantial evidence.

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:48.810
Besides, this kind of story
is a double-edged sword.

00:22:48.810 --> 00:22:54.700
If he is in fact connected to the royal family,
his well-being might be endangered.

00:22:54.700 --> 00:22:56.890
What does Luneberg himself say ?

00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:58.840
He has neither
affirmed nor denied it.

00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:02.680
He's ignoring it completely,
at least on the surface.

00:23:02.680 --> 00:23:04.760
That's what I thought.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:09.420
But it's a completely different story
if Luneberg himself spread the rumor.

00:23:09.970 --> 00:23:11.730
Lord Reinhard...

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:19.530
What a scheming bastard - to use his bloodline instead of his talents or abilities as his weapon.

00:23:19.530 --> 00:23:24.300
It's not completely certain that
Luneberg himself spread the rumor.

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:26.890
That's true.

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:30.160
But he might do
something like that.

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:31.680
He can't be underestimated.

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:37.120
Reinhard himself wants to
succeed to a Count's family.

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:43.090
But that is only as a means to establish a
stepping-stone on his way to his ultimate goal.

00:23:43.930 --> 00:23:48.050
With each step he takes, he must gain
experience and grow, but at the same time...

00:23:48.050 --> 00:23:51.380
...he'll also have to enhance
and secure his social position.

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:56.780
To this end, he plans to take advantage
of a Count's title if it benefits him.

00:23:58.270 --> 00:23:59.890
Say, Kircheis...

00:23:59.890 --> 00:24:00.950
Yes ?

00:24:00.950 --> 00:24:02.780
I feel rotten.

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:05.750
Rooted on rotten soil,
the trees will also rot.

00:24:05.750 --> 00:24:09.330
I hope the next campaign
will be planned soon.

00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:14.250
Then I won't have to stay in this rotten
place and I will be promoted, too.

00:24:16.590 --> 00:24:17.370
Hey !

00:24:18.710 --> 00:24:23.480
If conservative aristocrats or pacifists heard
that, they'd be outraged, Lord Reinhard.

00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:28.730
Though Kircheis worried about it,
if anyone else besides him heard it...

00:24:28.730 --> 00:24:30.880
...they would probably
just laugh at impudence.

00:24:31.710 --> 00:24:33.230
In other words...

00:24:33.230 --> 00:24:37.900
...it was, speaking from an objective
point of view, merely a laughable dream.

00:24:38.680 --> 00:24:45.000
This was an occurrence on June 18th,
Space Year 794, Empire Year 485.

00:24:40.980 --> 00:24:47.080
Candidate for Succeeding a Count's Family

